Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
>In my current game I found a great item; "a blessed -3 elven dagger"!

I'd *expect* that to be a bones item, actually (just not actually on the
pile).  Monster possessions created via mongets() are generated using
mksobj().  mksobj(), generating a weapon, does one of three things:

1 in 11: blessed, with a positive spe.
1 in 11: cursed, with a negative spe.
9 in 11: zero spe, with a 10% chance of being non-uncursed (50/50
blessed/cursed).

Various beings then have certain special effects applied:
* Demons never receive blessed *anything*.
* Lawful minions never receive cursed objects, objects with negative
  spe, or damaged objects.
* mplayers have their swords (but no other objects) given a spe in the
  range +3 ... +6. (There's further faffery with mplayers, I think.)
* There are cases in mongets() for dealing with the invocation
  implements. This includes the Book of the Dead, which is bizarre, as
  the BotD is not generated in Rodney's inventory, but instead on the
  floor at his feet. (If it were to be generated by mongets(), the BotD
  would always be cursed when you found it.)
* Princes of any sort have their weapons given a minimum spe of +1,
  and their armour given a minimum spe of +0.

(On a side note, I've just noticed something: Rodney is generated
asleep, but the hell hound in the room with him is not.  As a result,
Rodney being generated asleep is singularly pointless, since the hell
hound will start moving around long before the player even enters the
tower, let alone breaches the wall of Rodney's meditation room.)
